course: dictionary
lesson: 9982
title: Teaspoon: a spoon and a measure
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A teaspoon is a small spoon for stirring tea or coffee, and for eating some foods. Recipes also use it as a measure. Look at the context: «One can of ordinary cola has about seven teaspoons of sugar» means seven spoonfuls of sugar, not seven small spoons.
explain: In a recipe, «tsp» is the short form for teaspoon, and «tbsp» is the short form for tablespoon. Three teaspoons make one tablespoon. Medicine works the same way, but there a teaspoon is exactly 5 millilitres.
explain: Be careful with medicine. Always use the measuring spoon or syringe that comes with the medicine, not a kitchen spoon, because kitchen spoons come in different sizes. A «level teaspoon» is flat on top, but a «heaped teaspoon» has a pile on top, so it holds more.
fact: A teaspoon is a small spoon, and it is also a measure of how much it holds.
fact: A teaspoon holds about 5 millilitres.
fact: The short form is «tsp», and «tbsp» is a tablespoon.
fact: Three teaspoons make one tablespoon.
fact: Bees make honey one drop at a time: «one worker makes only about a twelfth of a teaspoon in her life».
exercise: «One can of ordinary cola has about seven teaspoons of sugar.» How many teaspoons of sugar does it have? | *Seven | Two | Seventeen | Twelve
exercise: What does a teaspoon measure in medicine? | About 500 millilitres | *About 5 millilitres | About 1 kilogram | About 50 litres
exercise: How many teaspoons make one tablespoon? | 2 | 4 | 10 | *3
test: A «level teaspoon» is flat on top. What does level mean here? | Very small | Full to the brim | Hot from the stove | *Flat on top, with no pile
test: Why should you use the measuring spoon that comes with medicine? | Measuring spoons taste better | *Kitchen spoons vary in size | Kitchen spoons are always too big | Kitchen spoons are too shiny
exam: Which is the short form for teaspoon in a recipe? | *tsp | tea | tbsp | spoon
